# X visual: Plate (full-bleed)

Default generated look for @piselliii tweet images (tables, screenshot grids, proof collages). **Not** Chalk Noir (that stays rare — see JARVIS).

## One sentence

The image **is** the plate. X rounds the corners. Never draw a second rounded card inside.

## Canvas

- Full-bleed fill: `#0a0a0a` (or very near — not pure `#000` void around a floating panel)
- Square image corners in the file (no rounded-rect “app card” chrome)
- One continuous surface edge-to-edge — padding is margin *inside* the plate, not a black frame outside it

## Layout

- **One composition** on one plate. Adapt the *grid* to the job (2-col proof, 4-col name table, stack of shots) — do not invent a new visual system per task
- Screenshots / crops sit **flush on the plate** (optional 1px hairline `#1c1c1c`). No nested rounded mini-cards, no glass panels, no drop shadows per tile
- Labels = typography on the plate (handle + status above/beside the shot), not “card headers” with their own background blocks
- Thin rules OK (`#1c1c1c`) for row/column structure. No heavy borders, no badge pills, no glow

## Type

- Clean sans (system Arial / SF). High contrast: titles near white, body `#d2d2d2`, labels `#6e6e6e`
- Bold only for names / key tokens — not whole paragraphs
- Prefer short bullets over walls; must stay readable when X compresses on mobile

## Do

- Reference look: `assets/project-names-fullbleed-v2.png` (+ UA twin `…-v2-ua.png`)
- When user pastes screenshots: place them on the plate in a clear grid; status text as plain labels
- Keep monochrome unless the source screenshot itself needs color

## Don’t (this is the failure mode)

- Black canvas + floating rounded “plaques” / cards (box-in-box; X rounds again → double radius)
- A column of separate cards each wrapping one screenshot
- Dashboard / widget / glassmorphism / frosted panels
- Decorative outer frames, soft shadows, thick outlines around every asset
- Making the plate smaller than the canvas so a black margin shows in the feed

## Quick self-check before export

1. Sample the four image corners — same plate color, not pure black frame
2. Count “rounded containers” in the design — must be **0** (X supplies the only round)
3. Could you describe it as one slab, not a stack of widgets? If no → rebuild
